<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-New South Wales says drought has eased.</title>
<headline>RTRS-New South Wales says drought has eased.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The area of New South Wales which remained drought declared fell to 29 percent in October from 37 percent in September, the state government said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;This is the lowest level of drought we've seen in NSW since February 1996 when 28 percent of the state was in drought,&quot; state agriculture minister Richard Amery said in a statement.</p>
<p>Amery said up to four million hectares of winter cereal crops could be harvested in the state, valued at up to A$1 billion. Excellent rainfall and warm weather in September had allowed pastures to recover, he said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
